{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01ET6AuBtokwPUX6CbTWsegz", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://wikieyetracking.di.unito.it/wpcd/wp/u/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://dlab.epfl.ch/wikispeedia/wpcd/wp/u/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wisconsinexaminer.com/2025/07/04/for-july-4-the-declaration-of-independence/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://evri-delivery.blogto.com/july-4-1776-declaration-of-independence\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wisconsinexaminer.com/?p=40155\"}, {\"url\": \"https://americacomesalive.com/day_in_history/july-4-1776-declaration-independence/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://americacomesalive.com/?p=9475\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ligonduncan.com/max-mclean-reads-the-declaration-of-independence/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://dantesisofo.com/?p=36493\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:03:11.248Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "United States Declaration of Independence July 4 1776", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_012kN5k1qLQU4agPgPQMR5Md", "content": [{"title": "United States Declaration of Independence", "url": "https://wikieyetracking.di.unito.it/wpcd/wp/u/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence.htm"}, {"title": "United States Declaration of Independence", "url": "https://dlab.epfl.ch/wikispeedia/wpcd/wp/u/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence.htm"}, {"title": "For July 4: The Declaration of Independence", "url": "https://wisconsinexaminer.com/2025/07/04/for-july-4-the-declaration-of-independence/"}, {"title": "july 4 1776 declaration of independence", "url": "https://evri-delivery.blogto.com/july-4-1776-declaration-of-independence"}, {"title": "For July 4: The Declaration of Independence", "url": "https://wisconsinexaminer.com/?p=40155"}, {"title": "July 4, 1776 Declaration of Independence", "url": "https://americacomesalive.com/day_in_history/july-4-1776-declaration-independence/"}, {"title": "July 4, 1776 Declaration of Independence", "url": "https://americacomesalive.com/?p=9475"}, {"title": "IN CONGRESS, JULY 4, 1776", "url": "https://ligonduncan.com/max-mclean-reads-the-declaration-of-independence/"}, {"title": "July 4, 1776", "url": "https://dantesisofo.com/?p=36493"}]}, "The Second Continental Congress adopted the Declaration of Independence on July 4, 1776, in Philadelphia. Several sources describe it as a formal explanation of the colonies' break from Britain. One account says the vote for independence itself came on July 2, and July 4 marks the day Congress approved the final wording. The Declaration was ultimately a formal explanation of why Congress had voted on July 2 to declare independence from Great Britain.\n\nThomas Jefferson drafted the text. Adams persuaded the committee to select Thomas Jefferson to compose the original draft of the document, which congress would edit to produce the final version. A later engrossed copy bearing the delegates' signatures is on display in the National Archives in Washington, D.C.\n\nThe document declared the Thirteen Colonies independent of Britain, and it is now the basis for the national holiday. The Independence Day of the United States of America is celebrated on July 4, the day Congress approved the wording of the Declaration."], "durationSeconds": 4.505941624999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01ET6AuBtokwPUX6CbTWsegz", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_018EkG33PdRUTa3tNDJjCYCr", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grito_de_Dolores\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/event/Grito-de-Dolores\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mdzol.com/mundo/grito-dolores-5-mitos-y-verdades-del-hito-que-marca-el-inicio-la-independencia-mexico-n1337678/amp\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.mdzol.com/mundo/grito-dolores-5-mitos-y-verdades-del-hito-que-marca-el-inicio-la-independencia-mexico-n1337678\"}, {\"url\": \"https://laopinion.com/2025/09/15/grito-de-dolores-5-mitos-y-verdades-del-hito-que-marca-el-inicio-de-la-independencia-de-mexico/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.culturagenial.com/es/grito-de-dolores/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://signage.openstack.org/aanewss/el-grito-de-independencia-historia-y-significado.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thefinalwager.com/?p=13121\"}, {\"url\": \"https://simple.wikipedia.com/wiki/Grito_de_Dolores\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:03:14.643Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Mexico declared independence date 1810 Grito de Dolores", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01AUoeTxFF7g33kbVpuLicHy", "content": [{"title": "Grito de Dolores", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grito_de_Dolores"}, {"title": "Grito de Dolores", "url": "https://www.britannica.com/event/Grito-de-Dolores"}, {"title": "www.mdzol.com", "url": "https://www.mdzol.com/mundo/grito-dolores-5-mitos-y-verdades-del-hito-que-marca-el-inicio-la-independencia-mexico-n1337678/amp"}, {"title": "grito dolores 5 mitos y verdades del hito que marca el inicio la independencia mexico n1337678", "url": "https://www.mdzol.com/mundo/grito-dolores-5-mitos-y-verdades-del-hito-que-marca-el-inicio-la-independencia-mexico-n1337678"}, {"title": "Grito de Dolores: 5 mitos y verdades del hito que marca el inicio de la independencia de México", "url": "https://laopinion.com/2025/09/15/grito-de-dolores-5-mitos-y-verdades-del-hito-que-marca-el-inicio-de-la-independencia-de-mexico/"}, {"title": "El grito de Dolores y la independencia de México: resumen y contexto", "url": "https://www.culturagenial.com/es/grito-de-dolores/"}, {"title": "Uncover El Grito De Independencia: History & Meaning", "url": "https://signage.openstack.org/aanewss/el-grito-de-independencia-historia-y-significado.html"}, {"title": "thefinalwager.com", "url": "https://thefinalwager.com/?p=13121"}, {"title": "Grito de Dolores", "url": "https://simple.wikipedia.com/wiki/Grito_de_Dolores"}]}, "The Grito de Dolores took place on 16 September 1810. Miguel Hidalgo y Costilla, a parish priest in Dolores (now Dolores Hidalgo, Guanajuato), rang the church bell and issued the call to revolt that started the Mexican War of Independence. Britannica dates the cry to September 16, 1810. Wikipedia gives the same date and describes it as the start of the Mexican War of Independence.\n\nSome sources add nuance:\n- **Night of the 15th vs. the 16th:** Mexico's celebration is held on the night of 15 September. Spanish-language coverage based on historian Herrejón says the cry itself was likely given around six in the morning on the 16th. The night-time observance was tied to a later tradition, and documents from the First Federal Republic (1823–1835) already show a midnight commemoration on the 15th.\n- **Not a legal declaration:** One source notes that the cry was not a formal declaration of independence in the legal sense. Its exact wording is also unknown. Britannica says the exact text of this most famous of all Mexican speeches is not known.\n- **Aftermath:** Hidalgo was captured and executed on July 30, 1811, and the independence movement continued after his death."], "durationSeconds": 7.894468084, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_018EkG33PdRUTa3tNDJjCYCr", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
